{"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/Semirings\/documentation\/Semirings\/MaxPlusSemiring","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/Semirings\/documentation\/Semirings"]]},"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"major":0,"patch":0},"relationshipsSections":[{"kind":"relationships","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Semirings\/documentation\/Semirings\/SelectiveSemiring","doc:\/\/Semirings\/documentation\/Semirings\/Semiring","doc:\/\/Semirings\/SL","doc:\/\/Semirings\/s8CopyableP","doc:\/\/Semirings\/s23CustomStringConvertibleP","doc:\/\/Semirings\/SQ","doc:\/\/Semirings\/s9EscapableP","doc:\/\/Semirings\/SH","doc:\/\/Semirings\/s8SendableP","doc:\/\/Semirings\/s16SendableMetatypeP"],"type":"conformsTo","title":"Conforms To"}],"sections":[],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"platforms":["Linux"],"tokens":[{"kind":"attribute","text":"@frozen"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"MaxPlusSemiring"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"kind":"genericParameter","text":"Value"},{"kind":"text","text":"> "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"where"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Value"},{"kind":"text","text":" : "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"_SemiringScalar"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Value"},{"kind":"text","text":" : "},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:s13SignedNumericP","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"SignedNumeric"}],"languages":["swift"]}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"level":2,"text":"Overview","type":"heading","anchor":"overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"zero"},{"type":"text","text":" is −∞ ("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Int.min"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"-.infinity"},{"type":"text","text":"), "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"one"},{"type":"text","text":" is 0, ⊕ is "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"max"},{"type":"text","text":" and ⊗ is "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"+"},{"type":"text","text":". "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"<"},{"type":"text","text":" is the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"natural order, in which longer is better: "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"MaxPlusSemiring(9) < MaxPlusSemiring(2)"},{"type":"text","text":". The order"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"is the reverse of the values’, so "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"[a, b].max()"},{"type":"text","text":" is the shorter and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".min()"},{"type":"text","text":" the longer."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"⊗ is a closed sum. −∞ (the zero) absorbs every value, and any other sum traps on integer","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"overflow. A finite integer sum that lands exactly on ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".min"},{"text":" is the zero, so an edge of that","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"weight carries no path. The carrier is ℝ ∪ {−∞}, without +∞. No operation checks for NaN. The","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"ShortestPaths entry points trap on a NaN weight.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Longest paths exist where no cycle has a positive length: "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"dagShortestPaths"},{"type":"text","text":" gives them in an"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"acyclic graph, and Bellman–Ford returns "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"nil"},{"type":"text","text":" when a positive cycle is reachable. Dijkstra’s"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"algorithm needs every examined weight to be at most 0."}]},{"syntax":null,"type":"codeListing","code":["dag.dagShortestPaths(from: s) { MaxPlusSemiring(duration[$0]) }"]}]}],"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/semirings\/maxplussemiring"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"metadata":{"roleHeading":"Structure","symbolKind":"struct","remoteSource":{"fileName":